  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "AoE sleep all enemies with sustained damage",
    "skill1": "consume HP to stun nearby enemies, then leap to distant enemy to deal damage and stun again",
    "skill2": "transform on HP-loss threshold, recovering HP while dealing damage to nearby enemies",
    "skill3": "ATK grows after sleep cast is active",
    "skill4": "post-ultimate haste and damage reduction, with reduced cooldown on HP-sacrifice skill",
    "skill5": "extra secondary form use gained per assist or kill"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Tasi]] opens with AoE sleep that damages all enemies, then leaps to a distant foe for another damage-and-stun sequence. HP sacrifice triggers a transformation that recovers HP while damaging nearby enemies in the alternate form. ATK grows after sleep casts, and post-ultimate Haste tightens the rotation between cycles. Assists or kills grant extra secondary-form uses for longer pressure windows. Sleep-immune targets stall her control package before the forms can cycle.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Tasi]] threatens a late team-wide sleep, then leaps across the field to stun and ramp after each dream. At half HP she transforms into an invincible butterfly, so do not dump burst into that form; single-target pins also struggle as she relocates. Use lasting wide ultimates like [[Shemira]] or [[Frieren]], and catch the sleep wind-up with [[Lily May]] when it becomes interruptible. Cut butterfly recovery with [[filter:heal-inhibitor]] like [[Frieren]] or [[Gwyneth]]."
}
